KBM direct look: stand the title's camera correctors down.

Symptom: with RECOMP_KBM=1 the mouse look stutters the moment the player
moves -- A/D (strafe) and W/S (forward/back) alike -- and is smooth while
standing still.

Cause: the mouse delta is written straight to the local camera's yaw/pitch once
per pad poll (refs/xboxrecomp/src/input/xinput_device.c, kbm_state, look_direct).
While moving, the title runs two correctors of its own and both pull the view
back toward where the stick would have left it:

  tSimCamera::UpdateYaw (0x57560) calls ShouldAutoYaw (0x55740) and then
  rate-limits the yaw toward the movement heading (velocity at +0xB4 ->
  ArcTan4, step *0x491CB0 * *0x361FC8 through mathTrig::LerpAngle).

  tSimCamera::UpdatePitch (0x55450) recenters +0x114 toward (+0x124 + +0x104)
  every tick.

So the view advances with the mouse and is dragged back once per tick. Strafing
shows it strongest (heading far from the view); walking forward still shows it
because the pitch recenter is independent of the heading.

Patch, three hunks in this file:

1. ShouldAutoYaw returns 0 while scghost_kbm_no_autoyaw() says the mouse owns
   the camera. Stack-safe early return: leaf function, `ret 8`, hence
   `esp += 12`.
2. ShouldAutoYaw's own exit path stays as generated for the gamepad case.
3. UpdatePitch skips the moving-branch recenter (`goto loc_00055732`, the
   ordinary return) under the same guard, so the pitch the mouse set survives
   the tick.

src/recomp_kbm.c supplies the guard: RECOMP_KBM on, RECOMP_KBM_LOOK_DIRECT on;
RECOMP_KBM_NO_AUTOYAW=0 disables it (A/B).

Applied by scripts/26-apply-game-patches.sh; regenerated trees lose it.

diff --git a/recomp/game/src/recomp/gen/recomp_0006.c b/recomp/game/src/recomp/gen/recomp_0006.c
--- a/recomp/game/src/recomp/gen/recomp_0006.c
+++ b/recomp/game/src/recomp/gen/recomp_0006.c
@@ -7,6 +7,10 @@
 #include "recomp_funcs.h"
 #include <math.h>
 
+/* MANUAL PATCH (see recomp/game/MANUAL_PATCHES.md): KBM direct look owns the
+ * camera, so the title's stick correctors must stand down. */
+extern int scghost_kbm_no_autoyaw(void);
+
 /**
  * VIDSimplePlayer_startAudio_000504D0
  * Original: 0x000504D0 - 0x000504D8 (8 bytes, 2 insns)
@@ -16466,6 +16470,11 @@
     if ((((uint8_t)((uint8_t)(_fa) - (uint8_t)(_fb)) >> 7) == 0)) goto loc_00055732; /* jns: not sign (positive) */
 
 loc_000556C4: ;
+    /* MANUAL PATCH: KBM direct look. While moving, UpdatePitch recenters the
+     * pitch toward (+0x124 + +0x104) every tick; with the mouse owning the
+     * camera that is a second pull-back (the W/S case). Leave the pitch where
+     * the mouse put it and take the ordinary return path. */
+    if (scghost_kbm_no_autoyaw()) goto loc_00055732;
     _fa = (uint32_t)(HI8(eax)) & 0xFFu; _fb = (uint32_t)(0) & 0xFFu;
     _fas = (int32_t)(int8_t)(_fa); _fbs = (int32_t)(int8_t)(_fb); /* cmp HI8(eax), 0 (8-bit) */
     _cf = 0; /* nothing borrows from zero */
@@ -16530,6 +16539,14 @@
     int32_t _fas = 0, _fbs = 0;
     (void)_fa; (void)_fb; (void)_fas; (void)_fbs;
 
+    /* MANUAL PATCH: KBM direct look. Returning 0 here keeps UpdateYaw from
+     * turning the camera toward the movement heading between mouse polls. */
+    if (scghost_kbm_no_autoyaw()) {
+        eax = 0;
+        esp += 12;
+        return; /* ret 8 */
+    }
+
 loc_00055740: ;
     edx = MEM32(esp + 8);
     _fa = (uint32_t)(HI8(edx)) & 0xFFu; _fb = (uint32_t)(0x20) & 0xFFu;
